A window's route parameters on a target that serves no requests.

They are one cell of state -- the binding the window's scoped slot hands its
body -- so a target holds it wherever it holds the rest, and every one of
these fills it with the struct's zero because nothing here is answering a URL.
That is the same answer a Go route handler gives a field the path does not
name, arrived at from the other end.

`ir.Window.Params` is therefore an `*ir.Var` rather than the `*ir.Param` the
slot declares, and `CodegenCtx.ModelState` yields it beside the vars the
owners declare. Left out, the read compiled to `m.v.Pkg` against a Model with
no such field, on all three Go targets at once -- state the tree reads and no
owner declares is exactly what ModelState exists to prevent being answered
four separate times.

-- params.sngl --
import ui "sngl:ui"

output {
    go {
        bubbletea
        fyne
    }
    kotlin {
        android
    }
}

struct PageParams {
    pkg string
}

ui.window #home(title="t", href=`/p/{pkg}`, params=PageParams{}) {
    component content(v) {
        ui.text(value="pkg is {v.pkg}")
    }
}
